# uboot-board.config — t113-gameboy BOARD-level U-Boot .config fragment.
#
# Board facts (this board's wiring + on-board flash), applied on top of the host
# fragment (forge/defaults/uboot-host.config). board.conf lists both in
# UBOOT_CONFIG_FRAGMENTS. LINE ORDER IS SIGNIFICANT — see the SPI-NOR note below.
#
# Console on UART0/PE2-PE3 (our t113-breakout wiring). The stock mangopi defconfig
# puts the SPL console on UART3/PB6-PB7 (CONS_INDEX=4); CONS_INDEX=1 moves the SPL
# console pinmux to PE2/PE3. (U-Boot *proper*'s console is fixed separately by the
# uart0-console.dtsi control-DTB overlay — CONS_INDEX alone is a split-brain trap.)
CONFIG_CONS_INDEX=1

# SPI-NOR flash support (the `sf` command). The NOR boot path FEL-loads U-Boot proper
# and drives `sf probe`/`sf read` to pull kernel+DTB+initramfs out of the on-board
# W25Q128 (Winbond).
#
# LINE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING — each symbol gates the ones below it, so an out-of-order
# line is silently dropped by olddefconfig (and caught by verify_config_fragment):
#   MTD           gates the SPI-flash (`if MTD`) menu.
#   SPI           the top-level `menuconfig SPI` — DM_SPI/DM_SPI_FLASH are nested under it;
#                 without it the whole SPI subtree stays off (mangopi_mq_r leaves SPI off).
#   DM_SPI        driver-model SPI bus (depends on DM, which the defconfig sets); required by
#                 DM_SPI_FLASH.
#   DM_SPI_FLASH  driver-model SPI-flash (depends on DM_SPI).
#   SPI_SUNXI     the Allwinner SPI controller driver — the actual bus the W25Q128 hangs
#                 off; `sf probe` finds nothing without it.
CONFIG_MTD=y
CONFIG_SPI=y
CONFIG_DM_SPI=y
CONFIG_SPI_SUNXI=y
CONFIG_SPI_FLASH=y
CONFIG_DM_SPI_FLASH=y
CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_WINBOND=y
CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_SFDP_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_CMD_SF=y
